I am not familiar with Process model 80, but there are several issues here.
It could be that the bootstrapping technique or the correction are not identical.
Even if they are identical, without setting a seed you shouldn’t expect them to be identical. A seed allows you to set the random number generator. A bootstrapped sample is a done by taking a random sample with replacement from your data of size N (where N is the number of observations in your original data set). So, it’s stochastic and should vary.

How different are your results? Are your estimates the same just the CIs differ? Can you provide more info about Process model 80 as well as the R code your running and maybe a reproducible amount of data/code?

Chris

