MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

> I am trying to find code for the twostage CFA-  but am having difficulty finding the actual code.

Find examples on the help page:

?semTools::twostage

Actually, lavaan implements this method internally now (but now with auxiliary variables), so you do not need the semTools function.  See the ?lavOptions help page to find the options for the missing= argument.

fit <- cfa(HS.model, data=HolzingerSwineford1939, missing = "robust.two.stage")

> I've read to either use robust maximum likelihood estimation with the Satorra-Bentler chi-square correction  or   se = robust.huber.white '
> I thought the huber white was preferred, because we have some missing data with a large sample

Yes, that option is set using estimator="MLR" (asymptotically equivalent to MLM, but works with incomplete data).  But if you want 2-stage SEM, setting the missing="robust.two.stage" argument will automatically set the se= and test= arguments to be robust.

